WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.295
Part ten.

00:00:01.295 --> 00:00:04.290
DB Test Session and rollback for Adminer.

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:10.791
Testing often means changing data in the database, and cleaning up afterwards is a chore.

00:00:10.791 --> 00:00:13.831
If you use Adminer, Pocket QA does it for you.

00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:17.137
Here is Adminer, open on the Demo Books database.

00:00:17.137 --> 00:00:20.100
Pocket QA adds a small panel in the corner.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.402
Click Start and name the test session.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:31.667
Change the price of Mountain Roads from 18 to 21, with Adminer's own edit form.

00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:35.901
Or run some hand-written SQL: mark every Tech book out of stock.

00:00:39.433 --> 00:00:44.614
The Pocket QA panel records each changed row, with its value before and after.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:46.989
Test done?

00:00:46.989 --> 00:00:48.504
Click Roll back all.

00:00:48.504 --> 00:00:52.370
Pocket QA shows the exact SQL it will run to put the data back.

00:00:55.633 --> 00:01:01.033
And the data is back as it was before the test: a price of 18, stock as before.

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:02.521
Every session is kept.

00:01:02.521 --> 00:01:05.534
Open the DB Test Session page from the Tools tab.

00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:15.742
Each one lists its changes, the undo SQL, and a drift check.

00:01:15.767 --> 00:01:18.244
There's one more kind of test: APIs.

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:19.405
That's next.
